OL,3,GNEWSAWhy are so many four-year-olds not
OL,4,Apotty-trained before school?
OL,5,
OL,6,FFor some parents the countdown to
OL,7,Fstarting school means buying uniforms,
OL,8,Flabelling water bottles and trying to
OL,9,Fsqueeze in one last summer holiday.
OL,11,FFor others there is a more basic
OL,12,Fquestion to tackle: can their child use
OL,13,Fthe toilet on their own?
OL,15,FAccording to a survey by the charity
OL,16,FKindred Squared, almost a third of
OL,17,Fchildren starting school in the West
OL,18,FMidlands last year were not fully
OL,19,Ftoilet-trained and 42% of those
OL,20,Farriving in reception were deemed not
OL,21,Fschool-ready by primary school staff.
OL,23,APub: 11-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
